 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +17% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $57M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -9.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 29\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 87% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8724875453774327},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"